    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nit doesn't recognize html tags correctly.\r\n\r\ninstead of \r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-672+g33e1a8cd7 (nightly)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. ...\r\n\r\nIf you have a simple html, like\r\n\r\n```html\r\n    <div id=\"root\">\r\n      <p></p>\r\n      <div></div>\r\n    </div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nif you try to perform operations on the root div, like `dit` it should delete all the content of the root div.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n```html\r\n    <div id=\"root\">\r\n    </div>\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n it's gonna delete until the internal div (so matching the first ending div, instead of HIS ending dif) and you end up having\r\n\r\n```html\r\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\r\n    </div>\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2023-07-15T10:32:10Z",
